window.products.push({"id":680359,"name":"La Vie En Rose by Natasha Wescoat, 24x32-Inch Canvas Wall Art","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":66.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71y7BP4zXrL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","description":"This ready to hang, gallery-wrapped art piece features pink and purple French shops surrounded by flowers. Art is the Heritage of Michigan native Natasha Wescoat, who comes from a family of artists. Her work is an enigmatic mix of colors and moving worlds filled with fantasy characters and dreamy landscapes, surely inspired by her childhood spent playing music and playing in the countryside. Known widely for her iconic jeweled trees tm, which hang in private and corporate collections worldwide, Natasha has retained this sense of whimsy and brightness in all of her work. She cites influences by Gustav Klimt, Vincent Van Gogh, and takashi murakami. Natasha's work is a mix of fantasy, surrealism, and pop art, which creates a unique and colorful, happy style that speaks to all ages. Giclee (jee-clay) is an advanced printmaking process for creating high quality fine art reproductions. The attainable excellence that giclee printmaking affords makes the reproduction virtually indistinguishable from the original piece. The result is wide acceptance of giclee by galleries, museums, and private collectors. Gallery wrap is a method of stretching an artist's canvas so that the canvas wraps around the sides and is secured a hidden, wooden frame. This method of stretching and preparing a canvas allows for a frameless presentation of the finished painting.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71y7BP4zXrL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Trademark Fine Art","source_asin":"B071VXZY14","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-680359","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B071VXZY14","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B071VXZY14","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
window.products.push({"id":680360,"name":"Luxury Large Handmade Glass Vase - Decorated with a Large Crystal from Swarovski® and Sandblasted Tulip Flower – Golden Gift Box – Diamond Collection ","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71eDVVKAWjL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"ANNA'S EXCLUSIVE DECOR DIAMOND Collection Hand-crafted and decorated finest quality glassware with Swarovski Crystal Elements. About this item This unique centerpiece has been carefully handcrafted and decorated in Poland - famous for its long history of hand-made glass production. The exceptional quality of this product is achieved with time-honoured blown glass techniques that are executed manually by skilled local glassblowers. Combining excellent workmanship with the latest technology, design and decoration techniques allows the creation of elegant centerpieces that are unique in their appeal. Glass products from Poland are famous and generate interest among customers all over the world. About the process The following three stages of the manufacturing process are executed manually, making each product unique: Stage 1: several minerals including silica sand and soda limestone are carefully measured and melted in a furnace at temperatures reaching 1700°C. Stage 2: a skilled glassblower gathers molten glass at the end of a hollow tube, mouth-blows into the tube while rotating it, using various tools and gravity to create a variety of forms, including vases, bowls, decanters etc. Bubbles of air can sometimes get trapped within the molten glass (and are occasionally visible in finished products) which is an acceptable and authentic part of handmade, mouth-blown glass. After achieving the desired shape, the glassblower cools the molten glass object down. Stage 3: an experienced artisan decorates the glass items using various decorative techniques. Depending on the desired result, the item is sandblasted and/or engraved and a Swarovski crystal element is carefully attached in a designated place to create a unique glassware product.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71eDVVKAWjL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Anna's Exclusive Decor","source_asin":"B084MKYR46","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-680360","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B084MKYR46","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B084MKYR46","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
